            "review_title": "Review at Alfresco - Vincom Ngô Quyền Đà Nẵng",
            "review_text": "Mashajo\nKaliningrad, Russia11599 contributions\n30\nLunch at Tz\nJul 2025 • Solo\nOnce at Vincom Plaza, she was looking for a place to eat, and she decided to go into this cafe. The attraction was that European cuisine was here - you wanted something familiar. The establishment is in the food court area: several tables and a bar in the middle. There's a lot of discount and promotional advertising at the entrance. Employees aren't very friendly, but English is spoken, so explaining yourself isn't a problem. I ordered quesadillas and shell soup in hot sauce. It came in pretty quickly - 20 minutes later. Quesadilla was served first: it doesn't look good, the portion is small, it tastes fine, no fascination. A portion of the shells was also scarce, but they tasted good. The service is very unobtrusive. A regular cafe for a quick snack in the food court, without much of an experience.\nRead more\nTranslated from Russian\nShow original\nWritten December 9, 2025",
